I should note first that any patch to implement mail on Windows NetHack must
necessarily break bones and save compatibility.  The official binary does
not implement even the fake mail daemon.

The mail feature first appeared in Hack 1.0.2.  In those days of yore, Hack
was most often played on Unix systems with text-only terminals.  Modern
GUIs existed on Macs, of course, but were still rare in the Unix world. 
Thus only one program could be visible at a time.  Mail notification was a
useful feature in any program, whether it had anything to do with mail or
not.

On Windows boxes, mail notification is only a win for those who prefer to
play full screen.  If you play in a window, you can always have your copy
of Thunderbird or Outlook or what-have-you running.

